OrionLayer open fix 71 — the hidden engine's animation waits
============================================================

Work order 212 (Part C, Data's decision 1: after fix 79). orion2re on
`orionlayer-local`, on top of open fix 79. Every line under ORION2RE_EXT.

Every battle animation waited its 55 ms frames in a window nobody sees, and
the engine speaks only from `Get_Input_`: an animated action's events reached
the client only after it had been played unseen (2.5 s for the Stellar
Converter). `timer::Release_Time_` now returns at once while a battle is live,
the window hidden, a client connected and no input poll came since the last
wait — an animation frame, not the input loop's own tick. Two exceptions keep
their waits: a timed wait for input (`fields::Timed_Wait_For_Input_` with a
timeout, the timed message box: it counts its time in waits), and the shield
flare's own poll (`Draw_Shield_` ends in `fields::Get_Input_`, beams.cpp)
does not count as the input loop's. Fix 79 makes it harmless for the sound:
the client plays every battle sound on its own clock, so a skipped wait cuts
no fade. With F12 or without a client the engine waits as before.

